Here is how to compile and run hello.b in the dmr directory.
Log in as dmr/dmr.
Lines starting with @ are the Unix prompt, type what is given.
Lines with no leading @ are output you should see.
The assembly step takes a while, it assembles the entire B runtime.

If this is the first B program you are compiling:
@ ln system bop.s
@ ln system brt.s

Then:

@ b hello.b hello.s
@ as bop.s brt.s hello.s
I
II
bop.s   
brt.s    
hello.s 
@ a.out
Hello, World!

